{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-1","title":"Ezekiel 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Ezekiel's commission. 6 His instruction. 9 The roll of his heavy prophecy.</p>\n<p>Son. 3,6,8; 3:1,4,10,17; 4:1; 5:1; 7:2; 12:3; 13:2; 14:3,13; 15:2; 16:2 17:2; 20:3; 37:3; Ps 8:4; Da 8:17; Mt 16:13-16; Joh 3:13,16 stand. 1:28; Da 10:11,19; Mt 17:7; Ac 9:6; 26:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-2","title":"Ezekiel 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>3:12,14,24; 36:27; Nu 11:25,26; Jud 13:25; 1Sa 16:13; Ne 9:30 Joe 2:28,29; Re 11:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-3","title":"Ezekiel 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I send. 3:4-8; 2Ch 36:15,16; Isa 6:8-10; Jer 1:7; 7:2; 25:3-7; 26:2-6; 36:2 Mr 12:2-5; Lu 24:47,48; Joh 20:21,22; Ro 10:15 a rebellious nation. Heb. rebellious nations. 16:1-63; 20:1-49; 23:1-49 rebelled. 20:18-30; Nu 20:10; 32:13,14; De 9:24,27; 1Sa 8:7,8; 2Ki 17:17-20 Ezr 9:7; Ne 9:16-18,26,33-35; Ps 106:16-21,28,32-40; Jer 3:25 Jer 16:11,12; 44:21; Da 9:5-13; Ac 7:51</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-4","title":"Ezekiel 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>they. 3:7; De 10:16; 31:27; 2Ch 30:8; 36:13; Ps 95:8; Isa 48:4; Jer 3:3 Jer 5:3; 6:15; 8:12; Mt 10:16 impudent. Heb. hard of face. Pr 21:29 Thus. 1Ki 22:14; Jer 26:2,3; Ac 20:26,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-5","title":"Ezekiel 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>whether. 7; 3:10,11,27; Mt 10:12-15; Ac 13:46; Ro 3:3; 2Co 2:15-17 yet. 3:19; 33:9,33; Lu 10:10-12; Joh 15:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-6","title":"Ezekiel 2:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>be not. 3:8,9; 2Ki 1:15; Isa 51:12; Jer 1:8,17; Mic 3:8; Mt 10:28; Lu 12:4 Ac 4:13,19,29; Eph 6:19; Php 1:28; 2Ti 1:7 briers. or, rebels. 2Sa 23:6,7; Isa 9:18; Jer 6:28; Mic 7:4 scorpions. Lu 10:19; Re 9:3-6 though they. 3:9,26,27; Pr 30:13,14; Isa 51:7; Jer 18:18; Am 7:10-17; Heb 11:27 1Pe 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-7","title":"Ezekiel 2:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>thou. 3:10,17; Jer 1:7,17; 23:28; 26:2; Jon 3:2; Mt 28:20 whether. 5 most rebellious. Heb. rebellion.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-8","title":"Ezekiel 2:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Be. Le 10:3; Nu 20:10-13,24; 1Ki 13:21,22; Isa 50:5; 1Pe 5:3 open. 3:1-3,10; Jer 15:16; 1Ti 4:14-16; Re 10:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-9","title":"Ezekiel 2:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>an hand. 8:3; Jer 1:9; Da 5:5; 10:10,16-18 a roll. All ancient books were written so as to be rolled up: hence{volumen,} a volume, from {volvo,} I roll.</p>\n<p>3:1; Heb 10:7; Re 5:1-5; 10:8-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-2-10","title":"Ezekiel 2:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>spread. Isa 30:8-11; Hab 2:2 was written within.Contrary to the state of rolls in general, which are written on the inside only.</p>\n<p>lamentations. Isa 3:11; Jer 36:29-32; Re 8:13; 9:12; 11:14</p>"}]}